{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And I will remove My hand.</b> וְאַעֲדֵי יָת דִּבְרַת יְקָרִי — when I remove the irradiation of My glory from before your face, to go from there and beyond." "<b>And you shall see My back.</b> He showed him the knot of tefillin (Berakhot 7a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The Aramaic opening (וראית את אחרי as rendered by Onkelos) is quoted in the language of the Targum: דִּבְרַת יְקָרִי = 'the splendor of My glory.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:26.636993100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}